// tobira driver plugin protocol, version 1.
//
// A plugin is a `tobira-driver-<name>` binary that hashicorp/go-plugin starts
// with protocol version 1 and AllowedProtocols grpc. It serves the Driver
// service below. The messages mirror package github.com/xavidop/tobira/driver
// one to one; the comments name the Go type each message carries.
//
// # Edition and strings
//
// The file uses edition 2023 with implicit field presence (proto3 behaviour)
// and utf8_validation NONE. Database text is not always valid UTF-8 (a Redis
// key, a bytea cast to text, a latin1 column), and a driver.Value must cross
// the boundary byte for byte, so no string field is validated. Readers in
// other languages must treat string fields as possibly invalid UTF-8.
//
// # Field numbering
//
// Numbers are stable for the life of v1. A field is never renumbered and a
// number is never reused: a removed field becomes `reserved` (number and
// name). New fields take the next free number in their message. Oneof
// members share their message's number space. An incompatible change is a
// new package, tobira.plugin.v2.
//
// # Handles
//
// Open returns a ConnHandle and Begin a TxHandle. Both are opaque ids the
// plugin chooses; the host only echoes them back. One plugin process serves
// many connections.
//
// # Capabilities
//
// DriverInfo.capabilities and OpenResponse.capabilities use the
// driver.Capability strings ("browser", "mutator", "explainer",
// "transactor", "vector_searcher", "timeseries_reader", "graph_reader",
// "completer", "exporter", "watcher", plus the declared guarantee
// "readonly"). The host never calls an RPC whose capability the plugin did
// not advertise; a plugin answers such a call with UNIMPLEMENTED.
//
// # Errors
//
// A failed RPC returns a gRPC status whose details carry one ErrorInfo. Its
// kind is driver.KindName of the error ("not_found", "read_only", ...), and
// the host rebuilds a *driver.Error from it. Messages are redacted by the
// plugin with the ConnConfig, and redacted again by the host.
//
// # Result streams
//
// Query, Browse, TxQuery, Similar and Range stream ResultFrames: one
// `columns` frame, then zero or more `rows` frames of 1 to 256 rows, then
// one `stats` frame. A multi-statement result (driver.MultiResultSet)
// repeats that sequence once per result set. A stream that ends without a
// stats frame is an error.
//
// # Limits
//
// gRPC messages are capped at 16 MiB. The host also caps each Value at
// 1 MiB encoded, a result at 4096 columns, every name (column, key,
// native type, zone) at 64 KiB, nesting at 64 levels, Stats at 256
// warnings and 256 notices of at most 64 KiB each and a 64 KiB next
// cursor, and rejects anything larger.

